      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is closed for skiing today, with the spring southwest wind returning above the operating threshold for chairlifts, and no improvement forecast as the wind is expected to increase slightly into the afternoon. There's been 6 cm of new snow in the past 24 hours, holding the natural base at 112 cm; it's currently -3°C with winds around 40 km/h gusting to 79 km/h, with a few snow showers forecast to lower to 1000m alongside strong southwesterly winds. The Junior Nationals Ski + Snowboard X has been postponed due to the weather. No lifts and runs are open today. The access road is chain-free, with an active road hazard advisory in place. The resort plans to try again tomorrow, with the spring Pines Shuttle and bus schedule beginning 1 October. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 0 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
